        "rtf_4wHnU8": {
          "type": "rtf",
          "settings": {
            "richtext_content": "<h1>Career Highlights</h1><p><strong>Fight Record</strong><br/>20 fights • 19 wins • 13 KOs</p><h3>2019</h3><p>Callum made his professional debut against Elvis Dube, securing a points victory.</p><h3>2022</h3><p>Callum claimed his first professional title, defeating Ben Ridings to win the Central Area Super-Middleweight Championship.</p><h3>2023</h3><p>Callum made his BOXXER debut with a TKO win over Celso Neves, before adding victories over Boris Crighton and Jose de Jesus Macias.</p><h3>2024</h3><p>On 3 August, Callum defeated Zak Chelli at Oakwell Stadium to become British and Commonwealth Super-Middleweight Champion.</p><h3>2025</h3><p>Callum successfully defended his British and Commonwealth titles against Steed Woodall and Elvis Ahorgah before stopping Ivan Zucco to become European Super-Middleweight Champion. He finished the year with his first professional defeat, losing his titles to Troy Williamson by 10th-round TKO.</p><h3>2026</h3><p>Eight months later, Callum returned to face Williamson in a rematch at the First Direct Arena in Leeds. He won by unanimous decision after 12 rounds, avenging his only career defeat and reclaiming the British and Commonwealth Super-Middleweight titles.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
